                  Firsthand history: Visitors gather in a subterranean bunker room for a briefing on how underground hospitals, kitchens, and command rooms functioned.
                </figcaption>
              </figure>

              <div class="bg-white p-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 shadow-xs space-y-2">
                <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">The Return Trip Catch</div>
                <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
                  Getting to Cu Chi independently is straightforward—booking a Grab car from downtown Saigon takes two minutes. Getting <em>back</em>, however, is another matter. Rural Cu Chi, particularly around Ben Duoc (70 km out), has very few ride-hailing drivers looking for return fares into the city. If you rely on an app to get home, you risk waiting an hour or negotiating an inflated cash fare. The smoothest independent approach is hiring a private car for the round trip with waiting time included.
                </p>
