                Practical Information For Visiting Cu Chi Tunnels
              </h2>
            </div>

            <div class="text-slate-700 text-[15.5px] leading-relaxed space-y-4">
              <div class="space-y-4">
                <div class="bg-white p-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 shadow-xs space-y-2">
                  <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">1. Admission & Opening Hours</div>
                  <ul class="text-xs text-slate-600 space-y-1.5 list-disc pl-4">
                    <li><strong>Operating Hours:</strong> 07:00 AM – 5:00 PM daily.</li>
                    <li><strong>Official 2026 Admission Fees:</strong> For international visitors, the Cu Chi Tunnels Management Board announced an all-inclusive entrance fee of <strong>135,000 VND per person</strong> effective February 1, 2026 (35,000 VND relic admission + 100,000 VND guide and service fee). Always check the official website before travelling in case of updates.</li>
                    <li><strong>Mobility Assistance:</strong> On-site electric shuttle carts are available for visitors with mobility needs; inquire at the entrance ticket counter.</li>
                    <li><strong>Steamed Cassava Snack:</strong> Every ticket includes a serving of freshly steamed cassava dipped in crushed peanuts, sesame seeds, and salt, served alongside hot tea at the Hoang Cam kitchen pavilion.</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>

                <div class="bg-white p-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 shadow-xs space-y-2">
                  <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">2. On-Site Shooting Range</div>
                  <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
                    Both Ben Dinh and Ben Duoc operate sports firing ranges where visitors can purchase live rounds to fire wartime rifles (AK-47, M16). If you are looking for a quiet, contemplative visit, be aware that gunfire echoes through nearby sections of the woods. Tell your guide upfront if you prefer to steer clear of the shooting range area entirely.
                  </p>
                </div>

                <div class="bg-white p-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 shadow-xs space-y-2">
                  <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">3. Transportation & Trip Planning Tips</div>
                  <ul class="text-xs text-slate-600 space-y-1.5 list-disc pl-4">
                    <li><strong>Time Budget:</strong> Plan for roughly 5 to 6 hours door-to-door for a private morning visit from central Ho Chi Minh City. Driving time is typically 1.5 hours each way to Ben Dinh, and 1.5 to 2 hours to Ben Duoc depending on morning highway traffic.</li>
                    <li><strong>Don't Combine Cu Chi with the Mekong Delta on the Same Day:</strong> Avoid the temptation to book the ubiquitous "Cu Chi + Mekong Delta in 1 Day" tour package. Cramming both into a single day means spending 5 to 6 hours stuck on highways, leaving only a rushed, superficial hour or two at each destination. Instead, consider booking a <a href="/tour/full-day-mekong-delta-tour-ben-tre-my-tho" class="text-amber-800 hover:text-amber-900 font-semibold underline underline-offset-2 decoration-amber-300">dedicated full-day Mekong Delta tour</a> on a separate day for a far richer experience.</li>
                    <li><strong>What to Wear:</strong> Wear lightweight, breathable clothing and sturdy closed-toe walking shoes suitable for red dirt forest paths. If you plan to crawl through the tunnels, wear darker clothes you don't mind getting dusty.</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
